WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.700
The second skill is measuring distance, and the tool is your dividers.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.775
Look at the diagram.

3
00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:11.325
Open the dividers so one point sits on each end of your line.

4
00:00:11.575 --> 00:00:17.500
Then carry them, without changing the opening, to the latitude scale on the side of the chart.

5
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.600
Read the minutes and tenths between the points.

6
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:27.375
One minute of latitude is one nautical mile, so five point three minutes is five point three miles.

7
00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:29.325
Two cautions.

8
00:00:29.575 --> 00:00:33.075
First, the Mercator chart stretches as you go north.

9
00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:36.025
So where on the side scale do you measure?

10
00:00:37.025 --> 00:00:38.825
Level with your work.

11
00:00:39.075 --> 00:00:42.275
Not at the top of the chart, and not at the bottom.

12
00:00:42.525 --> 00:00:46.350
Second, never use the scale across the top or bottom.

13
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.525
That’s longitude, and a minute of longitude isn’t a mile.
